      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "626896097f038e52a9200bb5",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "622940c4c639cf1f585fb239",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e59bc346312bf2d549f33ab|full_name}: LOD for world objects and terrain are a thing in well designed worlds. It actually doesn't take much to implement them. Just a lot of tedious work doing it for each object.\nUE5 actually does this for world meshes automatically, which allows for you to basically throw in entire photogrammetry scans.\nIf LOD were a non default safety setting people could adjust, anything that didn't have LOD could just default to fallback. So for example, I opt-in to only see avatars at LOD3 when super far away. If your avatar doesn't support LOD, then I see your avatar as fallback for all LOD.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
